{
  "$comment": "Side-by-side pairs of docs/QUALITY.md §2: every home and exploration site a native source frame shows (HUD on screen, docs/ART.md §1.1; punch-ins never), captured by `shot` (its storage, which unlocks the survivors, its steps, then the numeric look-at point in sim tiles, the floor, and `lookZoom`, the zoom amount of src/contracts/look.js zoomFov: 0 = 60° vFOV … 1 = 50°; the rest of the pose is src/contracts/look.js) reaching its `conditions` (day, hour, weather and scene, asserted from the game state by tests/visual.test.js), and judged on the `judge` list against `measured` within `tolerances`. `from` is the phase the pair is due. `nearest: true` marks a target with no native frame of its own, paired with the nearest native frame of the same kind of space. `descriptors.requires` must all hold for a 4 (they cumulate); `mayShow` are things the source shows that the recreation may add. Targets no native frame shows are `unpaired`, with why.",
  "schema": "survival-logs/side-by-side@2",
  "tolerances": {
    "vFovDeg": 1,
    "pitchDeg": 1,
    "yawDeg": 2,
    "valueCodes": 5,
    "paletteDeltaE2000": 8,
    "lightDeg": 15,
    "relativeAlbedoL": 5
  },
  "judges": {
    "camera": "tools/targets/camera.py on the capture: vFOV within ±1°, pitch within ±1°, yaw within ±2° of measured.camera",
    "value": "the median luma of the same region of the capture within ±5 codes of measured.value.median",
    "palette": "each of the capture's 3 dominant CIELAB colours (same method) within ΔE2000 8 of its nearest measured.palette colour",
    "light": "the key light of the capture (look.js rig) within 15° of measured.light in azimuth and in elevation",
    "relativeAlbedo": "the L* gaps between the 3 dominant colours of the capture within 5 of those of the source"
  },
